# WYSiteIWYG is an editor application that lives in /edit/. The public site it
# manages — root-level pages, generated section/tag directories, uploaded and
# imported assets — is content/output, not application source. This repo is the
# canonical source for the app, so it tracks the app and project infrastructure
# only; generated site content is kept out.

# Editor / OS noise (also matches nested copies)
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log
*.swp
*.swo

# Ignore everything at the repo root by default, then re-include just the app
# and project infrastructure. Anything else at the root (generated public pages,
# /assets/, local tooling such as /.claude/, and internal HANDOFF*.md dev notes)
# is intentionally untracked.
/*
!/.gitignore
!/.gitattributes
!/.htaccess
!/README.md
!/DEPLOYMENT.md
!/LICENSE
!/edit/
!/.github/

# Per-install configuration and credentials must never enter the repository,
# even if the root allowlist above is broadened later.
/.claude/
/doc/
/HANDOFF*.md
/OPUS_PROMPT.md
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.local.php
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/*.jks
**/*.keystore
**/id_rsa
**/id_dsa
**/id_ecdsa
**/id_ed25519
